19.993618\n  Converged: False after 3000 iterations\n\nRestart 5/10\n  Forward KL: 0.005 (error: 9.994687)\n  Backward KL: 0.005 (error: 9.994512)\n  Total error: 19.989198\n  Converged: False after 3000 iterations\n\nRestart 6/10\n  Forward KL: 2.288 (error: 7.711866)\n  Backward KL: 10.007 (error: 0.007302)\n  Total error: 7.719168\n  Converged: False after 3000 iterations\n\nRestart 7/10\n  Forward KL: 0.982 (error: 9.018283)\n  Backward KL: 10.000 (error: 0.000000)\n  Total error: 9.018283\n  Converged: False after 3000 iterations\n\nRestart 8/10\n  Forward KL: 1.083 (error: 8.917452)\n  Backward KL: 10.010 (error: 0.010430)\n  Total error: 8.927882\n  Converged: False after 3000 iterations\n\nRestart 9/10\n  Forward KL: 0.004 (error: 9.995585)\n  Backward KL: 0.004 (error: 9.995644)\n  Total error: 19.991229\n  Converged: False after 3000 iterations\n\nRestart 10/10\n  Forward KL: 0.006 (error: 9.993590)\n  Backward KL: 0.006 (error: 9.993667)\n  Total error: 19.987257\n  Converged: False after 3000 iterations\n\n==================================================\nFINAL RESULTS:\nForward KL divergence: 2.288134\nBackward KL divergence: 10.007302\nTarget: 10.0\nForward error: 7.711866\nBackward error: 0.007302\nWithin tolerance: False\n\nDistribution properties:\nSum of probabilities: 1.0000000000\nAll probabilities >= 0: True\nMax probability: 0.998290\nMin probability: 0.0000000000\nNumber of zero probabilities: 1\nSmall test failed. Need to debug the algorithm.\nForward KL error: 7.711866\nBackward KL error: 0.007302", "extras": {"command": "python find_distribution.py", "metadata": {"exit_code": 0, "pid": -1, "username": "root", "hostname": "rack-ge107-ya-20250517193277", "working_dir": "/app", "py_interpreter_path": "/opt/openhands-venv/bin/python", "prefix": "", "suffix": "\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]"}, "hidden": false}, "success": true}
{"id": 43, "timestamp": "2025-12-19T16:17:41.833886", "source": "agent", "message": "", "action": "edit", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "str_replace_editor", "tool_call_id": "toolu_20", "model_response": {"id": "msg_vrtx_011Gb8LeYL7cuoPLk66VFNAp", "created": 1766161061, "model": "claude-sonnet-4", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "I see the issue. The optimization is getting stuck because achieving both high KL divergences simultaneously requires a very specific type of distribution. Let me try a more analytical approach based on understanding the mathematical relationship between these KL divergences.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"command\": \"create\", \"path\": \"/app/analytical_solution.py\", \"file_text\": \"\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport math\\n\\ndef forward_kl(p, u):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Calculate KL(P||U) = \\u03a3 P(i) * log(P(i) / U(i))\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    epsilon = 1e-15\\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\\n    return np.sum(p * np.log(p_safe / u_safe))\\n\\ndef backward_kl(p, u):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Calculate KL(U||P) = \\u03a3 U(i) * log(U(i) / P(i))\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    epsilon = 1e-15\\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\\n    return np.sum(u * np.log(u_safe / p_safe))\\n\\ndef create_analytical_distribution(vocab_size, target_kl=10.0):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Create a distribution analytically based on the constraint.\\n    \\n    For both KL divergences to be equal to target_kl, we need a specific structure.\\n    Let's try a distribution where most probability mass is concentrated on a few elements.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    # Start with the insight that for high KL divergences, we need:\\n    # 1. Some probabilities much higher than uniform (1/V)\\n    # 2. Some probabilities much lower than uniform\\n    \\n    # Let's try a power-law like distribution\\n    # First, let's solve for a simpler case: what if we have just two types of probabilities?\\n    # - k elements with high probability p_high\\n    # - (V-k) elements with low probability p_low\\n    \\n    # The constraints are:\\n    # k * p_high + (V-k) * p_low = 1\\n    # KL(P||U) = k * p_high * log(p_high * V) + (V-k) * p_low * log(p_low * V) = target_kl\\n    # KL(U||P) = k * (1/V) * log(1/(V * p_high)) + (V-k) * (1/V) * log(1/(V * p_low)) = target_kl\\n    \\n    # This is still complex. Let me try a different approach.\\n    # Let's use the fact that for uniform distribution: KL(P||U) = H(U) - H(P) + log(V)\\n    # where H is entropy.\\n    \\n    # Try a parametric approach: exponential distribution in log space\\n    \\n    best_dist = None\\n    best_error = float('inf')\\n    \\n    # Try different numbers of \\\"peaked\\\" elements\\n    for k in [1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, min(1000, vocab_size // 10)]:\\n        if k >= vocab_size:\\n            continue\\n            \\n        # Try different concentration levels\\n        for alpha in np.logspace(0, 4, 20):  # from 1 to 10000\\n            \\n            # Create distribution: k elements get high prob, rest get low prob\\n            p = np.ones(vocab_size) * (1.0 / vocab_size)  # Start uniform\\n            \\n            # Concentrate probability on first k elements\\n            high_prob = alpha / vocab_size\\n            low_prob = (1.0 - k * high_prob) / (vocab_size - k)\\n            \\n            if high_prob <= 0 or low_prob <= 0 or high_prob > 1:\\n                continue\\n                \\n            p[:k] = high_prob\\n            p[k:] = low_prob\\n            \\n            # Normalize just to be safe\\n            p = p / np.sum(p)\\n            \\n            if not np.all(p > 0):\\n                continue\\n            \\n            u = np.ones(vocab_size) / vocab_size\\n            fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\\n            bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\\n            \\n            error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\\n            \\n            if error < best_error:\\n                best_error = error\\n                best_dist = p.copy()\\n                best_fkl = fkl\\n                best_bkl = bkl\\n                \\n                # Print if we found a good solution\\n                if error < 0.1:\\n                    print(f\\\"Good candidate: k={k}, alpha={alpha:.2f}\\\")\\n                    print(f\\\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.3f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.3f}\\\")\\n                    print(f\\\"  Error: {error:.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    return best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl\\n\\ndef create_exponential_distribution(vocab_size, target_kl=10.0):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Try creating an exponential-like distribution\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    best_dist = None\\n    best_error = float('inf')\\n    \\n    # Try different decay rates for exponential distribution\\n    for decay_rate in np.logspace(-3, 2, 50):  # From 0.001 to 100\\n        \\n        # Create exponential distribution\\n        indices = np.arange(vocab_size)\\n        log_probs = -decay_rate * indices\\n        \\n        # Convert to probabilities\\n        p = np.exp(log_probs)\\n        p = p / np.sum(p)\\n        \\n        u = np.ones(vocab_size) / vocab_size\\n        fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\\n        bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\\n        \\n        error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\\n        \\n        if error < best_error:\\n            best_error = error\\n            best_dist = p.copy()\\n            best_fkl = fkl\\n            best_bkl = bkl\\n            \\n            if error < 0.1:\\n                print(f\\\"Exponential candidate: decay={decay_rate:.4f}\\\")\\n                print(f\\\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.3f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.3f}\\\")\\n                print(f\\\"  Error: {error:.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    return best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl\\n\\ndef find_target_distribution(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0, tolerance=0.001):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Find target distribution using analytical approaches\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"Finding analytical solution for vocab_size={vocab_size}, target_kl={target_kl}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Tolerance: {tolerance}\\\")\\n    \\n    # Try different analytical approaches\\n    approaches = [\\n        (\\\"Two-level distribution\\\", create_analytical_distribution),\\n        (\\\"Exponential distribution\\\", create_exponential_distribution),\\n    ]\\n    \\n    best_solution = None\\n    best_error = float('inf')\\n    \\n    for name, method in approaches:\\n        print(f\\\"\\\\nTrying {name}...\\\")\\n        \\n        dist, fkl, bkl = method(vocab_size, target_kl)\\n        \\n        if dist is not None:\\n            fkl_error = abs(fkl - target_kl)\\n            bkl_error = abs(bkl - target_kl)\\n            total_error = fkl_error + bkl_error\\n            \\n            print(f\\\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f} (error: {fkl_error:.6f})\\\")\\n            print(f\\\"  Backward KL: {bkl:.6f} (error: {bkl_error:.6f})\\\")\\n            print(f\\\"  Total error: {total_error:.6f}\\\")\\n            \\n            if total_error < best_error:\\n                best_error = total_error\\n                best_solution = (dist, fkl, bkl)\\n                \\n                if fkl_error <= tolerance and bkl_error <= tolerance:\\n                    print(f\\\"Found solution within tolerance!\\\")\\n                    break\\n    \\n    if best_solution is None:\\n        print(\\\"No valid solution found\\\")\\n        return None, 0, 0\\n        \\n    p, fkl, bkl = best_solution\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"=\\\"*50)\\n    print(f\\\"FINAL RESULTS:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Forward KL divergence: {fkl:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Backward KL divergence: {bkl:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Target: {target_kl}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Forward error: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Backward error: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Within tolerance: {abs(fkl - target_kl) <= tolerance and abs(bkl - target_kl) <= tolerance}\\\")\\n    \\n    # Verify it's a valid probability distribution\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\nDistribution properties:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Sum of probabilities: {np.sum(p):.10f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"All probabilities >= 0: {np.all(p >= 0)}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Max probability: {np.max(p):.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Min probability: {np.min(p):.10f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Number of very small probabilities: {np.sum(p < 1e-10)}\\\")\\n    \\n    return p, fkl, bkl\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    # Test with small vocabulary first\\n    print(\\\"=\\\" * 50)\\n    print(\\\"Testing analytical approach with small vocabulary (V=10)\\\")\\n    print(\\\"=\\\" * 50)\\n    test_dist, test_fkl, test_bkl = find_target_distribution(vocab_size=10, target_kl=10.0)\\n    \\n    tolerance = 0.001\\n    target_kl = 10.0\\n    \\n    if test_dist is not None and abs(test_fkl - target_kl) <= tolerance and abs(test_bkl - target_kl) <= tolerance:\\n        print(\\\"Small test succeeded! Proceeding with full vocabulary...\\\")\\n        \\n        print(\\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"=\\\" * 50)\\n        print(\\\"Finding target distribution (V=150,000)\\\")\\n        print(\\\"=\\\" * 50)\\n        \\n        # Find the target distribution\\n        distribution, fkl, bkl = find_target_distribution()\\n        \\n        if distribution is not None and abs(fkl - target_kl) <= tolerance and abs(bkl - target_kl) <= tolerance:\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\nSuccess! Found distribution within tolerance.\\\")\\n            # Save the distribution\\n            np.save('/app/dist.npy', distribution)\\n            print(\\\"Distribution saved to /app/dist.npy\\\")\\n        else:\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\nFailed to find distribution within tolerance for large vocabulary.\\\")\\n            if distribution is not None:\\n                print(f\\\"Best errors - Forward: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f}, Backward: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f}\\\")\\n    else:\\n        print(\\\"Small test failed with analytical approach.\\\")\\n        if test_dist is not None:\\n            print(f\\\"Forward KL error: {abs(test_fkl - target_kl):.6f}\\\")\\n            print(f\\\"Backward KL error: {abs(test_bkl - target_kl):.6f}\\\")\\n\\n\"}", "name": "str_replace_editor"}, "id": "toolu_20", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 2937, "prompt_tokens": 22768, "total_tokens": 25705, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}, "extra_tokens_details": {"CacheCreationInputTokens": 22765}}, "service_tier": null}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "llm_metrics": {"accumulated_cost": 0.0, "max_budget_per_task": null, "accumulated_token_usage": {"model": "default", "prompt_tokens": 235418, "completion_tokens": 11594, "cache_read_tokens": 30710, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "context_window": 0, "per_turn_token": 25705, "response_id": ""}, "costs": [], "response_latencies": [], "token_usages": []}, "args": {"path": "/app/analytical_solution.py", "command": "create", "file_text": "\nimport numpy as np\nimport math\n\ndef forward_kl(p, u):\n    \"\"\"Calculate KL(P||U) = Σ P(i) * log(P(i) / U(i))\"\"\"\n    epsilon = 1e-15\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\n    return np.sum(p * np.log(p_safe / u_safe))\n\ndef backward_kl(p, u):\n    \"\"\"Calculate KL(U||P) = Σ U(i) * log(U(i) / P(i))\"\"\"\n    epsilon = 1e-15\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\n    return np.sum(u * np.log(u_safe / p_safe))\n\ndef create_analytical_distribution(vocab_size, target_kl=10.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Create a distribution analytically based on the constraint.\n    \n    For both KL divergences to be equal to target_kl, we need a specific structure.\n    Let's try a distribution where most probability mass is concentrated on a few elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Start with the insight that for high KL divergences, we need:\n    # 1. Some probabilities much higher than uniform (1/V)\n    # 2. Some probabilities much lower than uniform\n    \n    # Let's try a power-law like distribution\n    # First, let's solve for a simpler case: what if we have just two types of probabilities?\n    # - k elements with high probability p_high\n    # - (V-k) elements with low probability p_low\n    \n    # The constraints are:\n    # k * p_high + (V-k) * p_low = 1\n    # KL(P||U) = k * p_high * log(p_high * V) + (V-k) * p_low * log(p_low * V) = target_kl\n    # KL(U||P) = k * (1/V) * log(1/(V * p_high)) + (V-k) * (1/V) * log(1/(V * p_low)) = target_kl\n    \n    # This is still complex. Let me try a different approach.\n    # Let's use the fact that for uniform distribution: KL(P||U) = H(U) - H(P) + log(V)\n    # where H is entropy.\n    \n    # Try a parametric approach: exponential distribution in log space\n    \n    best_dist = None\n    best_error = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try different numbers of \"peaked\" elements\n    for k in [1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, min(1000, vocab_size // 10)]:\n        if k >= vocab_size:\n            continue\n            \n        # Try different concentration levels\n        for alpha in np.logspace(0, 4, 20):  # from 1 to 10000\n            \n            # Create distribution: k elements get high prob, rest get low prob\n            p = np.ones(vocab_size) * (1.0 / vocab_size)  # Start uniform\n            \n            # Concentrate probability on first k elements\n            high_prob = alpha / vocab_size\n            low_prob = (1.0 - k * high_prob) / (vocab_size - k)\n            \n            if high_prob <= 0 or low_prob <= 0 or high_prob > 1:\n                continue\n                \n            p[:k] = high_prob\n            p[k:] = low_prob\n            \n            # Normalize just to be safe\n            p = p / np.sum(p)\n            \n            if not np.all(p > 0):\n                continue\n            \n            u = np.ones(vocab_size) / vocab_size\n            fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\n            bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\n            \n            error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\n            \n            if error < best_error:\n                best_error = error\n                best_dist = p.copy()\n                best_fkl = fkl\n                best_bkl = bkl\n                \n                # Print if we found a good solution\n                if error < 0.1:\n                    print(f\"Good candidate: k={k}, alpha={alpha:.2f}\")\n                    print(f\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.3f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.3f}\")\n                    print(f\"  Error: {error:.6f}\")\n    \n    return best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl\n\ndef create_exponential_distribution(vocab_size, target_kl=10.0):\n    \"\"\"Try creating an exponential-like distribution\"\"\"\n    \n    best_dist = None\n    best_error = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try different decay rates for exponential distribution\n    for decay_rate in np.logspace(-3, 2, 50):  # From 0.001 to 100\n        \n        # Create exponential distribution\n        indices = np.arange(vocab_size)\n        log_probs = -decay_rate * indices\n        \n        # Convert to probabilities\n        p = np.exp(log_probs)\n        p = p / np.sum(p)\n        \n        u = np.ones(vocab_size) / vocab_size\n        fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\n        bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\n        \n        error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\n        \n        if error < best_error:\n            best_error = error\n            best_dist = p.copy()\n            best_fkl = fkl\n            best_bkl = bkl\n            \n            if error < 0.1:\n                print(f\"Exponential candidate: decay={decay_rate:.4f}\")\n                print(f\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.3f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.3f}\")\n                print(f\"  Error: {error:.6f}\")\n    \n    return best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl\n\ndef find_target_distribution(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0, tolerance=0.001):\n    \"\"\"Find target distribution using analytical approaches\"\"\"\n    \n    print(f\"Finding analytical solution for vocab_size={vocab_size}, target_kl={target_kl}\")\n    print(f\"Tolerance: {tolerance}\")\n    \n    # Try different analytical approaches\n    approaches = [\n        (\"Two-level distribution\", create_analytical_distribution),\n        (\"Exponential distribution\", create_exponential_distribution),\n    ]\n    \n    best_solution = None\n    best_error = float('inf')\n    \n    for name, method in approaches:\n        print(f\"\\nTrying {name}...\")\n        \n        dist, fkl, bkl = method(vocab_size, target_kl)\n        \n        if dist is not None:\n            fkl_error = abs(fkl - target_kl)\n            bkl_error = abs(bkl - target_kl)\n            total_error = fkl_error + bkl_error\n            \n            print(f\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f} (error: {fkl_error:.6f})\")\n            print(f\"  Backward KL: {bkl:.6f} (error: {bkl_error:.6f})\")\n            print(f\"  Total error: {total_error:.6f}\")\n            \n            if total_error < best_error:\n                best_error = total_error\n                best_solution = (dist, fkl, bkl)\n                \n                if fkl_error <= tolerance and bkl_error <= tolerance:\n                    print(f\"Found solution within tolerance!\")\n                    break\n    \n    if best_solution is None:\n        print(\"No valid solution found\")\n        return None, 0, 0\n        \n    p, fkl, bkl = best_solution\n    \n    print(f\"\\n\" + \"=\"*50)\n    print(f\"FINAL RESULTS:\")\n    print(f\"Forward KL divergence: {fkl:.6f}\")\n    print(f\"Backward KL divergence: {bkl:.6f}\")\n    print(f\"Target: {target_kl}\")\n    print(f\"Forward error: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f}\")\n    print(f\"Backward error: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f}\")\n    print(f\"Within tolerance: {abs(fkl - target_kl) <= tolerance and abs(bkl - target_kl) <= tolerance}\")\n    \n    # Verify it's a valid probability distribution\n    print(f\"\\nDistribution properties:\")\n    print(f\"Sum of probabilities: {np.sum(p):.10f}\")\n    print(f\"All probabilities >= 0: {np.all(p >= 0)}\")\n    print(f\"Max probability: {np.max(p):.6f}\")\n    print(f\"Min probability: {np.min(p):.10f}\")\n    print(f\"Number of very small probabilities: {np.sum(p < 1e-10)}\")\n    \n    return p, fkl, bkl\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    # Test with small vocabulary first\n    print(\"=\" * 50)\n    print(\"Testing analytical approach with small vocabulary (V=10)\")\n    print(\"=\" * 50)\n    test_dist, test_fkl, test_bkl = find_target_distribution(vocab_size=10, target_kl=10.0)\n    \n    tolerance = 0.001\n    target_kl = 10.0\n    \n    if test_dist is not None and abs(test_fkl - target_kl) <= tolerance and abs(test_bkl - target_kl) <= tolerance:\n        print(\"Small test succeeded! Proceeding with full vocabulary...\")\n        \n        print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n        print(\"Finding target distribution (V=150,000)\")\n        print(\"=\" * 50)\n        \n        # Find the target distribution\n        distribution, fkl, bkl = find_target_distribution()\n        \n        if distribution is not None and abs(fkl - target_kl) <= tolerance and abs(bkl - target_kl) <= tolerance:\n            print(f\"\\nSuccess! Found distribution within tolerance.\")\n            # Save the distribution\n            np.save('/app/dist.npy', distribution)\n            print(\"Distribution saved to /app/dist.npy\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"\\nFailed to find distribution within tolerance for large vocabulary.\")\n            if distribution is not None:\n                print(f\"Best errors - Forward: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f}, Backward: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"Small test failed with analytical approach.\")\n        if test_dist is not None:\n            print(f\"Forward KL error: {abs(test_fkl - target_kl):.6f}\")\n            print(f\"Backward KL error: {abs(test_bkl - target_kl):.6f}\")\n\n", "old_str": null, "new_str": null, "insert_line": null, "content": "", "start": 1, "end": -1, "thought": "I see the issue. The optimization is getting stuck because achieving both high KL divergences simultaneously requires a very specific type of distribution. Let me try a more analytical approach based on understanding the mathematical relationship between these KL divergences.", "impl_source": "oh_aci"}}
