850000, Forward KL=9.708, Backward KL=1.897, Error=8.395054\n  Iter 34: alpha=0.850000, Forward KL=9.708, Backward KL=1.897, Error=8.395054\n  Iter 35: alpha=0.850000, Forward KL=9.708, Backward KL=1.897, Error=8.395054\n  Iter 36: alpha=0.850000, Forward KL=9.708, Backward KL=1.897, Error=8.395054\n\nFinal single-peak result:\n  Alpha: 0.87500000\n  Forward KL: 10.051822 (error: 0.051822)\n  Backward KL: 2.079342 (error: 7.920658)\n  Total error: 7.972480\n\nTrying two-peak distribution...\n  Best two-peak: k=5, alpha_total=0.980\n  Forward KL: 10.004735, Backward KL: 3.911516\n  Total error: 6.093219\n\nUsing two-peak solution (better)\n\n============================================================\nFINAL SOLUTION:\nForward KL divergence: 10.004735\nBackward KL divergence: 3.911516\nTarget: 10.0\nForward error: 0.004735\nBackward error: 6.088484\nTotal error: 6.093219\nWithin tolerance: False\n\nDistribution properties:\nSum of probabilities: 1.0000000000\nAll probabilities >= 0: True\nMax probability: 0.19600000\nMin probability: 0.0000001333\nEntropy: 1.913655\nNumber of elements with >1% of uniform prob: 150000\n\n⚠️  Solution found but not within strict tolerance\nForward KL error: 0.004735\nBackward KL error: 6.088484\nRequired tolerance: 0.001\nBest attempt saved to /app/dist.npy", "extras": {"command": "python final_solution.py", "metadata": {"exit_code": 0, "pid": -1, "username": "root", "hostname": "rack-ge107-ya-20250517193277", "working_dir": "/app", "py_interpreter_path": "/opt/openhands-venv/bin/python", "prefix": "", "suffix": "\n[The command completed with exit code 0.]"}, "hidden": false}, "success": true}
{"id": 61, "timestamp": "2025-12-19T16:20:57.561993", "source": "agent", "message": "", "action": "edit", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "str_replace_editor", "tool_call_id": "toolu_29", "model_response": {"id": "msg_vrtx_01Dj6qibSEYYVxuGa88E5P1q", "created": 1766161257, "model": "claude-sonnet-4", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "I can see that finding a distribution that satisfies both KL divergence constraints exactly to within the tolerance is extremely challenging. The forward KL is close (error: 0.005), but the backward KL is still far off. Let me try a more sophisticated approach using iterative refinement and better mathematical insight.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"command\": \"create\", \"path\": \"/app/precise_solution.py\", \"file_text\": \"\\n\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ndef forward_kl(p, u):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Calculate KL(P||U) = \\u03a3 P(i) * log(P(i) / U(i))\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    epsilon = 1e-15\\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\\n    return np.sum(p * np.log(p_safe / u_safe))\\n\\ndef backward_kl(p, u):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Calculate KL(U||P) = \\u03a3 U(i) * log(U(i) / P(i))\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    epsilon = 1e-15\\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\\n    return np.sum(u * np.log(u_safe / p_safe))\\n\\ndef iterative_solution(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0, tolerance=0.001):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Use iterative approach to find solution.\\n    \\n    Key insight: We need H(P) = log(V) - target_kl for forward KL constraint\\n    For V=150000, log(V) \\u2248 11.918, so H(P) should be \\u2248 1.918\\n    \\n    This means we need a very low entropy distribution.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"Iterative solution approach for V={vocab_size}\\\")\\n    \\n    V = vocab_size\\n    log_V = np.log(V)\\n    target_entropy = log_V - target_kl\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"log(V) = {log_V:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Target entropy H(P) = {target_entropy:.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    u = np.ones(V) / V\\n    \\n    # Strategy: Create a distribution with exactly the target entropy\\n    # and then adjust it to also satisfy the backward KL constraint\\n    \\n    # Start with a very peaked distribution\\n    # Use a mixture approach: some elements have high prob, others have minimal prob\\n    \\n    best_solution = None\\n    best_error = float('inf')\\n    \\n    # Try different numbers of \\\"active\\\" elements\\n    for num_active in [1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 30, 50, 100]:\\n        if num_active >= V:\\n            continue\\n            \\n        print(f\\\"\\\\nTrying {num_active} active elements...\\\")\\n        \\n        # Use iterative approach to find the right probabilities\\n        for iteration in range(50):\\n            # Create initial distribution with num_active equal probabilities\\n            p_active = 0.9 / num_active  # Start with 90% of prob mass on active elements\\n            p_inactive = 0.1 / (V - num_active)  # Rest distributed uniformly\\n            \\n            # Adjust based on iteration\\n            alpha = 0.8 + 0.19 * iteration / 49  # From 0.8 to 0.99\\n            \\n            p_active = alpha / num_active\\n            p_inactive = (1 - alpha) / (V - num_active)\\n            \\n            if p_inactive <= 0:\\n                continue\\n                \\n            p = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\\n            p[:num_active] = p_active\\n            \\n            # Normalize just to be sure\\n            p = p / np.sum(p)\\n            \\n            # Calculate KL divergences\\n            fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\\n            bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\\n            \\n            error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\\n            \\n            if error < best_error:\\n                best_error = error\\n                best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha)\\n                \\n                print(f\\\"  Better solution: alpha={alpha:.3f}, Forward KL={fkl:.3f}, Backward KL={bkl:.3f}, Error={error:.6f}\\\")\\n                \\n                if error < tolerance:\\n                    print(f\\\"  Found solution within tolerance!\\\")\\n                    break\\n    \\n    if best_solution is None:\\n        return None, 0, 0\\n        \\n    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\\n    \\n    # Try fine-tuning around the best solution found\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\nFine-tuning around best solution (num_active={num_active})...\\\")\\n    \\n    # More precise search around the best alpha\\n    alpha_center = alpha\\n    for delta in np.linspace(-0.05, 0.05, 100):\\n        test_alpha = alpha_center + delta\\n        if test_alpha <= 0 or test_alpha >= 1:\\n            continue\\n            \\n        p_active = test_alpha / num_active\\n        p_inactive = (1 - test_alpha) / (V - num_active)\\n        \\n        if p_inactive <= 0:\\n            continue\\n            \\n        p_test = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\\n        p_test[:num_active] = p_active\\n        p_test = p_test / np.sum(p_test)\\n        \\n        fkl_test = forward_kl(p_test, u)\\n        bkl_test = backward_kl(p_test, u)\\n        error_test = abs(fkl_test - target_kl) + abs(bkl_test - target_kl)\\n        \\n        if error_test < best_error:\\n            best_error = error_test\\n            best_solution = (p_test.copy(), fkl_test, bkl_test, num_active, test_alpha)\\n            \\n            if error_test < tolerance:\\n                print(f\\\"  Fine-tuning found solution within tolerance!\\\")\\n                print(f\\\"    Alpha={test_alpha:.6f}, Error={error_test:.6f}\\\")\\n                break\\n    \\n    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"\\\\nFinal result:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Number of active elements: {num_active}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Alpha (total prob on active elements): {alpha:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Probability per active element: {alpha/num_active:.8f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Probability per inactive element: {(1-alpha)/(V-num_active):.10f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f} (error: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f})\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Backward KL: {bkl:.6f} (error: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f})\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Total error: {best_error:.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    return p, fkl, bkl\\n\\ndef mathematical_approach(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Try to solve the mathematical constraint more directly.\\n    \\n    We know that for the forward KL:\\n    KL(P||U) = -H(P) + log(V) = target_kl\\n    So H(P) = log(V) - target_kl\\n    \\n    And for backward KL:\\n    KL(U||P) = -log(V) - (1/V) * \\u03a3 log(P(i)) = target_kl\\n    So (1/V) * \\u03a3 log(P(i)) = -log(V) - target_kl\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    V = vocab_size\\n    log_V = np.log(V)\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"Mathematical approach for V={V}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Required entropy: {log_V - target_kl:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Required mean log probability: {V*(-log_V - target_kl):.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    # Try to construct a distribution that satisfies both constraints\\n    # Use a power-law like distribution\\n    \\n    best_solution = None\\n    best_error = float('inf')\\n    \\n    # Try different power-law exponents\\n    for exponent in np.logspace(-3, 2, 100):  # From 0.001 to 100\\n        \\n        # Create power-law distribution\\n        indices = np.arange(1, V + 1)\\n        p = 1.0 / (indices ** exponent)\\n        p = p / np.sum(p)  # Normalize\\n        \\n        u = np.ones(V) / V\\n        fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\\n        bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\\n        \\n        error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\\n        \\n        if error < best_error:\\n            best_error = error\\n            best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, exponent)\\n    \\n    if best_solution is not None:\\n        p, fkl, bkl, exponent = best_solution\\n        print(f\\\"Best power-law: exponent={exponent:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  Error: {best_error:.6f}\\\")\\n        \\n        return p, fkl, bkl\\n    \\n    return None, 0, 0\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    print(\\\"Precise solution attempt\\\")\\n    print(\\\"=\\\"*60)\\n    \\n    # Try both approaches\\n    print(\\\"Approach 1: Iterative refinement\\\")\\n    dist1, fkl1, bkl1 = iterative_solution()\\n    \\n    print(\\\"\\\\nApproach 2: Mathematical/Power-law\\\")\\n    dist2, fkl2, bkl2 = mathematical_approach()\\n    \\n    # Choose the better solution\\n    error1 = abs(fkl1 - 10.0) + abs(bkl1 - 10.0) if dist1 is not None else float('inf')\\n    error2 = abs(fkl2 - 10.0) + abs(bkl2 - 10.0) if dist2 is not None else float('inf')\\n    \\n    if error1 < error2:\\n        if dist1 is not None:\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\nUsing iterative solution (error: {error1:.6f})\\\")\\n            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist1, fkl1, bkl1\\n        else:\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nNo valid solution found\\\")\\n            best_dist = None\\n    else:\\n        if dist2 is not None:\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\nUsing mathematical solution (error: {error2:.6f})\\\")\\n            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist2, fkl2, bkl2\\n        else:\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nNo valid solution found\\\")\\n            best_dist = None\\n    \\n    if best_dist is not None:\\n        tolerance = 0.001\\n        fkl_error = abs(best_fkl - 10.0)\\n        bkl_error = abs(best_bkl - 10.0)\\n        \\n        print(f\\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"=\\\"*60)\\n        print(f\\\"FINAL SOLUTION:\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Forward KL divergence: {best_fkl:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Backward KL divergence: {best_bkl:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Target: 10.0\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Forward error: {fkl_error:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Backward error: {bkl_error:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Within tolerance: {fkl_error <= tolerance and bkl_error <= tolerance}\\\")\\n        \\n        np.save('/app/dist.npy', best_dist)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\nDistribution saved to /app/dist.npy\\\")\\n        \\n        # Verification\\n        print(f\\\"Sum of probabilities: {np.sum(best_dist):.10f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Max probability: {np.max(best_dist):.8f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Min probability: {np.min(best_dist):.12f}\\\")\\n    else:\\n        print(\\\"\\\\nFailed to find any valid solution\\\")\\n\\n\\n\"}", "name": "str_replace_editor"}, "id": "toolu_29", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 3188, "prompt_tokens": 39724, "total_tokens": 42912, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}, "extra_tokens_details": {"CacheCreationInputTokens": 39721}}, "service_tier": null}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "llm_metrics": {"accumulated_cost": 0.0, "max_budget_per_task": null, "accumulated_token_usage": {"model": "default", "prompt_tokens": 522472, "completion_tokens": 24748, "cache_read_tokens": 104529, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "context_window": 0, "per_turn_token": 42912, "response_id": ""}, "costs": [], "response_latencies": [], "token_usages": []}, "args": {"path": "/app/precise_solution.py", "command": "create", "file_text": "\n\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef forward_kl(p, u):\n    \"\"\"Calculate KL(P||U) = Σ P(i) * log(P(i) / U(i))\"\"\"\n    epsilon = 1e-15\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\n    return np.sum(p * np.log(p_safe / u_safe))\n\ndef backward_kl(p, u):\n    \"\"\"Calculate KL(U||P) = Σ U(i) * log(U(i) / P(i))\"\"\"\n    epsilon = 1e-15\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\n    return np.sum(u * np.log(u_safe / p_safe))\n\ndef iterative_solution(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0, tolerance=0.001):\n    \"\"\"\n    Use iterative approach to find solution.\n    \n    Key insight: We need H(P) = log(V) - target_kl for forward KL constraint\n    For V=150000, log(V) ≈ 11.918, so H(P) should be ≈ 1.918\n    \n    This means we need a very low entropy distribution.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    print(f\"Iterative solution approach for V={vocab_size}\")\n    \n    V = vocab_size\n    log_V = np.log(V)\n    target_entropy = log_V - target_kl\n    \n    print(f\"log(V) = {log_V:.6f}\")\n    print(f\"Target entropy H(P) = {target_entropy:.6f}\")\n    \n    u = np.ones(V) / V\n    \n    # Strategy: Create a distribution with exactly the target entropy\n    # and then adjust it to also satisfy the backward KL constraint\n    \n    # Start with a very peaked distribution\n    # Use a mixture approach: some elements have high prob, others have minimal prob\n    \n    best_solution = None\n    best_error = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try different numbers of \"active\" elements\n    for num_active in [1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 30, 50, 100]:\n        if num_active >= V:\n            continue\n            \n        print(f\"\\nTrying {num_active} active elements...\")\n        \n        # Use iterative approach to find the right probabilities\n        for iteration in range(50):\n            # Create initial distribution with num_active equal probabilities\n            p_active = 0.9 / num_active  # Start with 90% of prob mass on active elements\n            p_inactive = 0.1 / (V - num_active)  # Rest distributed uniformly\n            \n            # Adjust based on iteration\n            alpha = 0.8 + 0.19 * iteration / 49  # From 0.8 to 0.99\n            \n            p_active = alpha / num_active\n            p_inactive = (1 - alpha) / (V - num_active)\n            \n            if p_inactive <= 0:\n                continue\n                \n            p = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\n            p[:num_active] = p_active\n            \n            # Normalize just to be sure\n            p = p / np.sum(p)\n            \n            # Calculate KL divergences\n            fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\n            bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\n            \n            error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\n            \n            if error < best_error:\n                best_error = error\n                best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha)\n                \n                print(f\"  Better solution: alpha={alpha:.3f}, Forward KL={fkl:.3f}, Backward KL={bkl:.3f}, Error={error:.6f}\")\n                \n                if error < tolerance:\n                    print(f\"  Found solution within tolerance!\")\n                    break\n    \n    if best_solution is None:\n        return None, 0, 0\n        \n    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\n    \n    # Try fine-tuning around the best solution found\n    print(f\"\\nFine-tuning around best solution (num_active={num_active})...\")\n    \n    # More precise search around the best alpha\n    alpha_center = alpha\n    for delta in np.linspace(-0.05, 0.05, 100):\n        test_alpha = alpha_center + delta\n        if test_alpha <= 0 or test_alpha >= 1:\n            continue\n            \n        p_active = test_alpha / num_active\n        p_inactive = (1 - test_alpha) / (V - num_active)\n        \n        if p_inactive <= 0:\n            continue\n            \n        p_test = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\n        p_test[:num_active] = p_active\n        p_test = p_test / np.sum(p_test)\n        \n        fkl_test = forward_kl(p_test, u)\n        bkl_test = backward_kl(p_test, u)\n        error_test = abs(fkl_test - target_kl) + abs(bkl_test - target_kl)\n        \n        if error_test < best_error:\n            best_error = error_test\n            best_solution = (p_test.copy(), fkl_test, bkl_test, num_active, test_alpha)\n            \n            if error_test < tolerance:\n                print(f\"  Fine-tuning found solution within tolerance!\")\n                print(f\"    Alpha={test_alpha:.6f}, Error={error_test:.6f}\")\n                break\n    \n    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\n    \n    print(f\"\\nFinal result:\")\n    print(f\"  Number of active elements: {num_active}\")\n    print(f\"  Alpha (total prob on active elements): {alpha:.6f}\")\n    print(f\"  Probability per active element: {alpha/num_active:.8f}\")\n    print(f\"  Probability per inactive element: {(1-alpha)/(V-num_active):.10f}\")\n    print(f\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f} (error: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f})\")\n    print(f\"  Backward KL: {bkl:.6f} (error: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f})\")\n    print(f\"  Total error: {best_error:.6f}\")\n    \n    return p, fkl, bkl\n\ndef mathematical_approach(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Try to solve the mathematical constraint more directly.\n    \n    We know that for the forward KL:\n    KL(P||U) = -H(P) + log(V) = target_kl\n    So H(P) = log(V) - target_kl\n    \n    And for backward KL:\n    KL(U||P) = -log(V) - (1/V) * Σ log(P(i)) = target_kl\n    So (1/V) * Σ log(P(i)) = -log(V) - target_kl\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    V = vocab_size\n    log_V = np.log(V)\n    \n    print(f\"Mathematical approach for V={V}\")\n    print(f\"Required entropy: {log_V - target_kl:.6f}\")\n    print(f\"Required mean log probability: {V*(-log_V - target_kl):.6f}\")\n    \n    # Try to construct a distribution that satisfies both constraints\n    # Use a power-law like distribution\n    \n    best_solution = None\n    best_error = float('inf')\n    \n    # Try different power-law exponents\n    for exponent in np.logspace(-3, 2, 100):  # From 0.001 to 100\n        \n        # Create power-law distribution\n        indices = np.arange(1, V + 1)\n        p = 1.0 / (indices ** exponent)\n        p = p / np.sum(p)  # Normalize\n        \n        u = np.ones(V) / V\n        fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\n        bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\n        \n        error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\n        \n        if error < best_error:\n            best_error = error\n            best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, exponent)\n    \n    if best_solution is not None:\n        p, fkl, bkl, exponent = best_solution\n        print(f\"Best power-law: exponent={exponent:.6f}\")\n        print(f\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.6f}\")\n        print(f\"  Error: {best_error:.6f}\")\n        \n        return p, fkl, bkl\n    \n    return None, 0, 0\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\"Precise solution attempt\")\n    print(\"=\"*60)\n    \n    # Try both approaches\n    print(\"Approach 1: Iterative refinement\")\n    dist1, fkl1, bkl1 = iterative_solution()\n    \n    print(\"\\nApproach 2: Mathematical/Power-law\")\n    dist2, fkl2, bkl2 = mathematical_approach()\n    \n    # Choose the better solution\n    error1 = abs(fkl1 - 10.0) + abs(bkl1 - 10.0) if dist1 is not None else float('inf')\n    error2 = abs(fkl2 - 10.0) + abs(bkl2 - 10.0) if dist2 is not None else float('inf')\n    \n    if error1 < error2:\n        if dist1 is not None:\n            print(f\"\\nUsing iterative solution (error: {error1:.6f})\")\n            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist1, fkl1, bkl1\n        else:\n            print(\"\\nNo valid solution found\")\n            best_dist = None\n    else:\n        if dist2 is not None:\n            print(f\"\\nUsing mathematical solution (error: {error2:.6f})\")\n            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist2, fkl2, bkl2\n        else:\n            print(\"\\nNo valid solution found\")\n            best_dist = None\n    \n    if best_dist is not None:\n        tolerance = 0.001\n        fkl_error = abs(best_fkl - 10.0)\n        bkl_error = abs(best_bkl - 10.0)\n        \n        print(f\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n        print(f\"FINAL SOLUTION:\")\n        print(f\"Forward KL divergence: {best_fkl:.6f}\")\n        print(f\"Backward KL divergence: {best_bkl:.6f}\")\n        print(f\"Target: 10.0\")\n        print(f\"Forward error: {fkl_error:.6f}\")\n        print(f\"Backward error: {bkl_error:.6f}\")\n        print(f\"Within tolerance: {fkl_error <= tolerance and bkl_error <= tolerance}\")\n        \n        np.save('/app/dist.npy', best_dist)\n        print(\"\\nDistribution saved to /app/dist.npy\")\n        \n        # Verification\n        print(f\"Sum of probabilities: {np.sum(best_dist):.10f}\")\n        print(f\"Max probability: {np.max(best_dist):.8f}\")\n        print(f\"Min probability: {np.min(best_dist):.12f}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"\\nFailed to find any valid solution\")\n\n\n", "old_str": null, "new_str": null, "insert_line": null, "content": "", "start": 1, "end": -1, "thought": "I can see that finding a distribution that satisfies both KL divergence constraints exactly to within the tolerance is extremely challenging. The forward KL is close (error: 0.005), but the backward KL is still far off. Let me try a more sophisticated approach using iterative refinement and better mathematical insight.", "impl_source": "oh_aci"}}
{"id": 62, "timestamp": "2025-12-19T16:20:57.592985", "source": "agent", "message": "I edited the file /app/precise_solution.py.", "cause": 61, "observation": "edit", "tool_call_metadata": {"function_name": "str_replace_editor", "tool_call_id": "toolu_29", "model_response": {"id": "msg_vrtx_01Dj6qibSEYYVxuGa88E5P1q", "created": 1766161257, "model": "claude-sonnet-4", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": null, "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "I can see that finding a distribution that satisfies both KL divergence constraints exactly to within the tolerance is extremely challenging. The forward KL is close (error: 0.005), but the backward KL is still far off. Let me try a more sophisticated approach using iterative refinement and better mathematical insight.", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": [{"index": 1, "function": {"arguments": "{\"command\": \"create\", \"path\": \"/app/precise_solution.py\", \"file_text\": \"\\n\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\ndef forward_kl(p, u):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Calculate KL(P||U) = \\u03a3 P(i) * log(P(i) / U(i))\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    epsilon = 1e-15\\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\\n    return np.sum(p * np.log(p_safe / u_safe))\\n\\ndef backward_kl(p, u):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Calculate KL(U||P) = \\u03a3 U(i) * log(U(i) / P(i))\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    epsilon = 1e-15\\n    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\\n    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\\n    return np.sum(u * np.log(u_safe / p_safe))\\n\\ndef iterative_solution(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0, tolerance=0.001):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Use iterative approach to find solution.\\n    \\n    Key insight: We need H(P) = log(V) - target_kl for forward KL constraint\\n    For V=150000, log(V) \\u2248 11.918, so H(P) should be \\u2248 1.918\\n    \\n    This means we need a very low entropy distribution.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"Iterative solution approach for V={vocab_size}\\\")\\n    \\n    V = vocab_size\\n    log_V = np.log(V)\\n    target_entropy = log_V - target_kl\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"log(V) = {log_V:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Target entropy H(P) = {target_entropy:.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    u = np.ones(V) / V\\n    \\n    # Strategy: Create a distribution with exactly the target entropy\\n    # and then adjust it to also satisfy the backward KL constraint\\n    \\n    # Start with a very peaked distribution\\n    # Use a mixture approach: some elements have high prob, others have minimal prob\\n    \\n    best_solution = None\\n    best_error = float('inf')\\n    \\n    # Try different numbers of \\\"active\\\" elements\\n    for num_active in [1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 30, 50, 100]:\\n        if num_active >= V:\\n            continue\\n            \\n        print(f\\\"\\\\nTrying {num_active} active elements...\\\")\\n        \\n        # Use iterative approach to find the right probabilities\\n        for iteration in range(50):\\n            # Create initial distribution with num_active equal probabilities\\n            p_active = 0.9 / num_active  # Start with 90% of prob mass on active elements\\n            p_inactive = 0.1 / (V - num_active)  # Rest distributed uniformly\\n            \\n            # Adjust based on iteration\\n            alpha = 0.8 + 0.19 * iteration / 49  # From 0.8 to 0.99\\n            \\n            p_active = alpha / num_active\\n            p_inactive = (1 - alpha) / (V - num_active)\\n            \\n            if p_inactive <= 0:\\n                continue\\n                \\n            p = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\\n            p[:num_active] = p_active\\n            \\n            # Normalize just to be sure\\n            p = p / np.sum(p)\\n            \\n            # Calculate KL divergences\\n            fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\\n            bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\\n            \\n            error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\\n            \\n            if error < best_error:\\n                best_error = error\\n                best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha)\\n                \\n                print(f\\\"  Better solution: alpha={alpha:.3f}, Forward KL={fkl:.3f}, Backward KL={bkl:.3f}, Error={error:.6f}\\\")\\n                \\n                if error < tolerance:\\n                    print(f\\\"  Found solution within tolerance!\\\")\\n                    break\\n    \\n    if best_solution is None:\\n        return None, 0, 0\\n        \\n    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\\n    \\n    # Try fine-tuning around the best solution found\\n    print(f\\\"\\\\nFine-tuning around best solution (num_active={num_active})...\\\")\\n    \\n    # More precise search around the best alpha\\n    alpha_center = alpha\\n    for delta in np.linspace(-0.05, 0.05, 100):\\n        test_alpha = alpha_center + delta\\n        if test_alpha <= 0 or test_alpha >= 1:\\n            continue\\n            \\n        p_active = test_alpha / num_active\\n        p_inactive = (1 - test_alpha) / (V - num_active)\\n        \\n        if p_inactive <= 0:\\n            continue\\n            \\n        p_test = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\\n        p_test[:num_active] = p_active\\n        p_test = p_test / np.sum(p_test)\\n        \\n        fkl_test = forward_kl(p_test, u)\\n        bkl_test = backward_kl(p_test, u)\\n        error_test = abs(fkl_test - target_kl) + abs(bkl_test - target_kl)\\n        \\n        if error_test < best_error:\\n            best_error = error_test\\n            best_solution = (p_test.copy(), fkl_test, bkl_test, num_active, test_alpha)\\n            \\n            if error_test < tolerance:\\n                print(f\\\"  Fine-tuning found solution within tolerance!\\\")\\n                print(f\\\"    Alpha={test_alpha:.6f}, Error={error_test:.6f}\\\")\\n                break\\n    \\n    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"\\\\nFinal result:\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Number of active elements: {num_active}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Alpha (total prob on active elements): {alpha:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Probability per active element: {alpha/num_active:.8f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Probability per inactive element: {(1-alpha)/(V-num_active):.10f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f} (error: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f})\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Backward KL: {bkl:.6f} (error: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f})\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"  Total error: {best_error:.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    return p, fkl, bkl\\n\\ndef mathematical_approach(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Try to solve the mathematical constraint more directly.\\n    \\n    We know that for the forward KL:\\n    KL(P||U) = -H(P) + log(V) = target_kl\\n    So H(P) = log(V) - target_kl\\n    \\n    And for backward KL:\\n    KL(U||P) = -log(V) - (1/V) * \\u03a3 log(P(i)) = target_kl\\n    So (1/V) * \\u03a3 log(P(i)) = -log(V) - target_kl\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    \\n    V = vocab_size\\n    log_V = np.log(V)\\n    \\n    print(f\\\"Mathematical approach for V={V}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Required entropy: {log_V - target_kl:.6f}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"Required mean log probability: {V*(-log_V - target_kl):.6f}\\\")\\n    \\n    # Try to construct a distribution that satisfies both constraints\\n    # Use a power-law like distribution\\n    \\n    best_solution = None\\n    best_error = float('inf')\\n    \\n    # Try different power-law exponents\\n    for exponent in np.logspace(-3, 2, 100):  # From 0.001 to 100\\n        \\n        # Create power-law distribution\\n        indices = np.arange(1, V + 1)\\n        p = 1.0 / (indices ** exponent)\\n        p = p / np.sum(p)  # Normalize\\n        \\n        u = np.ones(V) / V\\n        fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\\n        bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\\n        \\n        error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\\n        \\n        if error < best_error:\\n            best_error = error\\n            best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, exponent)\\n    \\n    if best_solution is not None:\\n        p, fkl, bkl, exponent = best_solution\\n        print(f\\\"Best power-law: exponent={exponent:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"  Error: {best_error:.6f}\\\")\\n        \\n        return p, fkl, bkl\\n    \\n    return None, 0, 0\\n\\nif __name__ == \\\"__main__\\\":\\n    print(\\\"Precise solution attempt\\\")\\n    print(\\\"=\\\"*60)\\n    \\n    # Try both approaches\\n    print(\\\"Approach 1: Iterative refinement\\\")\\n    dist1, fkl1, bkl1 = iterative_solution()\\n    \\n    print(\\\"\\\\nApproach 2: Mathematical/Power-law\\\")\\n    dist2, fkl2, bkl2 = mathematical_approach()\\n    \\n    # Choose the better solution\\n    error1 = abs(fkl1 - 10.0) + abs(bkl1 - 10.0) if dist1 is not None else float('inf')\\n    error2 = abs(fkl2 - 10.0) + abs(bkl2 - 10.0) if dist2 is not None else float('inf')\\n    \\n    if error1 < error2:\\n        if dist1 is not None:\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\nUsing iterative solution (error: {error1:.6f})\\\")\\n            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist1, fkl1, bkl1\\n        else:\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nNo valid solution found\\\")\\n            best_dist = None\\n    else:\\n        if dist2 is not None:\\n            print(f\\\"\\\\nUsing mathematical solution (error: {error2:.6f})\\\")\\n            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist2, fkl2, bkl2\\n        else:\\n            print(\\\"\\\\nNo valid solution found\\\")\\n            best_dist = None\\n    \\n    if best_dist is not None:\\n        tolerance = 0.001\\n        fkl_error = abs(best_fkl - 10.0)\\n        bkl_error = abs(best_bkl - 10.0)\\n        \\n        print(f\\\"\\\\n\\\" + \\\"=\\\"*60)\\n        print(f\\\"FINAL SOLUTION:\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Forward KL divergence: {best_fkl:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Backward KL divergence: {best_bkl:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Target: 10.0\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Forward error: {fkl_error:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Backward error: {bkl_error:.6f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Within tolerance: {fkl_error <= tolerance and bkl_error <= tolerance}\\\")\\n        \\n        np.save('/app/dist.npy', best_dist)\\n        print(\\\"\\\\nDistribution saved to /app/dist.npy\\\")\\n        \\n        # Verification\\n        print(f\\\"Sum of probabilities: {np.sum(best_dist):.10f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Max probability: {np.max(best_dist):.8f}\\\")\\n        print(f\\\"Min probability: {np.min(best_dist):.12f}\\\")\\n    else:\\n        print(\\\"\\\\nFailed to find any valid solution\\\")\\n\\n\\n\"}", "name": "str_replace_editor"}, "id": "toolu_29", "type": "function"}], "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 3188, "prompt_tokens": 39724, "total_tokens": 42912, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 0, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}, "extra_tokens_details": {"CacheCreationInputTokens": 39721}}, "service_tier": null}, "total_calls_in_response": 1}, "content": "File created successfully at: /app/precise_solution.py", "extras": {"path": "/app/precise_solution.py", "prev_exist": false, "old_content": null, "new_content": null, "impl_source": "oh_aci", "diff": "--- /app/precise_solution.py\n+++ /app/precise_solution.py\n@@ -1,0 +2,253 @@\n+\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+\n+def forward_kl(p, u):\n+    \"\"\"Calculate KL(P||U) = Σ P(i) * log(P(i) / U(i))\"\"\"\n+    epsilon = 1e-15\n+    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\n+    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\n+    return np.sum(p * np.log(p_safe / u_safe))\n+\n+def backward_kl(p, u):\n+    \"\"\"Calculate KL(U||P) = Σ U(i) * log(U(i) / P(i))\"\"\"\n+    epsilon = 1e-15\n+    p_safe = np.maximum(p, epsilon)\n+    u_safe = np.maximum(u, epsilon)\n+    return np.sum(u * np.log(u_safe / p_safe))\n+\n+def iterative_solution(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0, tolerance=0.001):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Use iterative approach to find solution.\n+\n+    Key insight: We need H(P) = log(V) - target_kl for forward KL constraint\n+    For V=150000, log(V) ≈ 11.918, so H(P) should be ≈ 1.918\n+\n+    This means we need a very low entropy distribution.\n+    \"\"\"\n+\n+    print(f\"Iterative solution approach for V={vocab_size}\")\n+\n+    V = vocab_size\n+    log_V = np.log(V)\n+    target_entropy = log_V - target_kl\n+\n+    print(f\"log(V) = {log_V:.6f}\")\n+    print(f\"Target entropy H(P) = {target_entropy:.6f}\")\n+\n+    u = np.ones(V) / V\n+\n+    # Strategy: Create a distribution with exactly the target entropy\n+    # and then adjust it to also satisfy the backward KL constraint\n+\n+    # Start with a very peaked distribution\n+    # Use a mixture approach: some elements have high prob, others have minimal prob\n+\n+    best_solution = None\n+    best_error = float('inf')\n+\n+    # Try different numbers of \"active\" elements\n+    for num_active in [1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 10, 15, 20, 30, 50, 100]:\n+        if num_active >= V:\n+            continue\n+\n+        print(f\"\\nTrying {num_active} active elements...\")\n+\n+        # Use iterative approach to find the right probabilities\n+        for iteration in range(50):\n+            # Create initial distribution with num_active equal probabilities\n+            p_active = 0.9 / num_active  # Start with 90% of prob mass on active elements\n+            p_inactive = 0.1 / (V - num_active)  # Rest distributed uniformly\n+\n+            # Adjust based on iteration\n+            alpha = 0.8 + 0.19 * iteration / 49  # From 0.8 to 0.99\n+\n+            p_active = alpha / num_active\n+            p_inactive = (1 - alpha) / (V - num_active)\n+\n+            if p_inactive <= 0:\n+                continue\n+\n+            p = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\n+            p[:num_active] = p_active\n+\n+            # Normalize just to be sure\n+            p = p / np.sum(p)\n+\n+            # Calculate KL divergences\n+            fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\n+            bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\n+\n+            error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\n+\n+            if error < best_error:\n+                best_error = error\n+                best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha)\n+\n+                print(f\"  Better solution: alpha={alpha:.3f}, Forward KL={fkl:.3f}, Backward KL={bkl:.3f}, Error={error:.6f}\")\n+\n+                if error < tolerance:\n+                    print(f\"  Found solution within tolerance!\")\n+                    break\n+\n+    if best_solution is None:\n+        return None, 0, 0\n+\n+    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\n+\n+    # Try fine-tuning around the best solution found\n+    print(f\"\\nFine-tuning around best solution (num_active={num_active})...\")\n+\n+    # More precise search around the best alpha\n+    alpha_center = alpha\n+    for delta in np.linspace(-0.05, 0.05, 100):\n+        test_alpha = alpha_center + delta\n+        if test_alpha <= 0 or test_alpha >= 1:\n+            continue\n+\n+        p_active = test_alpha / num_active\n+        p_inactive = (1 - test_alpha) / (V - num_active)\n+\n+        if p_inactive <= 0:\n+            continue\n+\n+        p_test = np.ones(V) * p_inactive\n+        p_test[:num_active] = p_active\n+        p_test = p_test / np.sum(p_test)\n+\n+        fkl_test = forward_kl(p_test, u)\n+        bkl_test = backward_kl(p_test, u)\n+        error_test = abs(fkl_test - target_kl) + abs(bkl_test - target_kl)\n+\n+        if error_test < best_error:\n+            best_error = error_test\n+            best_solution = (p_test.copy(), fkl_test, bkl_test, num_active, test_alpha)\n+\n+            if error_test < tolerance:\n+                print(f\"  Fine-tuning found solution within tolerance!\")\n+                print(f\"    Alpha={test_alpha:.6f}, Error={error_test:.6f}\")\n+                break\n+\n+    p, fkl, bkl, num_active, alpha = best_solution\n+\n+    print(f\"\\nFinal result:\")\n+    print(f\"  Number of active elements: {num_active}\")\n+    print(f\"  Alpha (total prob on active elements): {alpha:.6f}\")\n+    print(f\"  Probability per active element: {alpha/num_active:.8f}\")\n+    print(f\"  Probability per inactive element: {(1-alpha)/(V-num_active):.10f}\")\n+    print(f\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f} (error: {abs(fkl - target_kl):.6f})\")\n+    print(f\"  Backward KL: {bkl:.6f} (error: {abs(bkl - target_kl):.6f})\")\n+    print(f\"  Total error: {best_error:.6f}\")\n+\n+    return p, fkl, bkl\n+\n+def mathematical_approach(vocab_size=150000, target_kl=10.0):\n+    \"\"\"\n+    Try to solve the mathematical constraint more directly.\n+\n+    We know that for the forward KL:\n+    KL(P||U) = -H(P) + log(V) = target_kl\n+    So H(P) = log(V) - target_kl\n+\n+    And for backward KL:\n+    KL(U||P) = -log(V) - (1/V) * Σ log(P(i)) = target_kl\n+    So (1/V) * Σ log(P(i)) = -log(V) - target_kl\n+    \"\"\"\n+\n+    V = vocab_size\n+    log_V = np.log(V)\n+\n+    print(f\"Mathematical approach for V={V}\")\n+    print(f\"Required entropy: {log_V - target_kl:.6f}\")\n+    print(f\"Required mean log probability: {V*(-log_V - target_kl):.6f}\")\n+\n+    # Try to construct a distribution that satisfies both constraints\n+    # Use a power-law like distribution\n+\n+    best_solution = None\n+    best_error = float('inf')\n+\n+    # Try different power-law exponents\n+    for exponent in np.logspace(-3, 2, 100):  # From 0.001 to 100\n+\n+        # Create power-law distribution\n+        indices = np.arange(1, V + 1)\n+        p = 1.0 / (indices ** exponent)\n+        p = p / np.sum(p)  # Normalize\n+\n+        u = np.ones(V) / V\n+        fkl = forward_kl(p, u)\n+        bkl = backward_kl(p, u)\n+\n+        error = abs(fkl - target_kl) + abs(bkl - target_kl)\n+\n+        if error < best_error:\n+            best_error = error\n+            best_solution = (p.copy(), fkl, bkl, exponent)\n+\n+    if best_solution is not None:\n+        p, fkl, bkl, exponent = best_solution\n+        print(f\"Best power-law: exponent={exponent:.6f}\")\n+        print(f\"  Forward KL: {fkl:.6f}, Backward KL: {bkl:.6f}\")\n+        print(f\"  Error: {best_error:.6f}\")\n+\n+        return p, fkl, bkl\n+\n+    return None, 0, 0\n+\n+if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n+    print(\"Precise solution attempt\")\n+    print(\"=\"*60)\n+\n+    # Try both approaches\n+    print(\"Approach 1: Iterative refinement\")\n+    dist1, fkl1, bkl1 = iterative_solution()\n+\n+    print(\"\\nApproach 2: Mathematical/Power-law\")\n+    dist2, fkl2, bkl2 = mathematical_approach()\n+\n+    # Choose the better solution\n+    error1 = abs(fkl1 - 10.0) + abs(bkl1 - 10.0) if dist1 is not None else float('inf')\n+    error2 = abs(fkl2 - 10.0) + abs(bkl2 - 10.0) if dist2 is not None else float('inf')\n+\n+    if error1 < error2:\n+        if dist1 is not None:\n+            print(f\"\\nUsing iterative solution (error: {error1:.6f})\")\n+            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist1, fkl1, bkl1\n+        else:\n+            print(\"\\nNo valid solution found\")\n+            best_dist = None\n+    else:\n+        if dist2 is not None:\n+            print(f\"\\nUsing mathematical solution (error: {error2:.6f})\")\n+            best_dist, best_fkl, best_bkl = dist2, fkl2, bkl2\n+        else:\n+            print(\"\\nNo valid solution found\")\n+            best_dist = None\n+\n+    if best_dist is not None:\n+        tolerance = 0.001\n+        fkl_error = abs(best_fkl - 10.0)\n+        bkl_error = abs(best_bkl - 10.0)\n+\n+        print(f\"\\n\" + \"=\"*60)\n+        print(f\"FINAL SOLUTION:\")\n+        print(f\"Forward KL divergence: {best_fkl:.6f}\")\n+        print(f\"Backward KL divergence: {best_bkl:.6f}\")\n+        print(f\"Target: 10.0\")\n+        print(f\"Forward error: {fkl_error:.6f}\")\n+        print(f\"Backward error: {bkl_error:.6f}\")\n+        print(f\"Within tolerance: {fkl_error <= tolerance and bkl_error <= tolerance}\")\n+\n+        np.save('/app/dist.npy', best_dist)\n+        print(\"\\nDistribution saved to /app/dist.npy\")\n+\n+        # Verification\n+        print(f\"Sum of probabilities: {np.sum(best_dist):.10f}\")\n+        print(f\"Max probability: {np.max(best_dist):.8f}\")\n+        print(f\"Min probability: {np.min(best_dist):.12f}\")\n+    else:\n+        print(\"\\nFailed to find any valid solution\")\n+\n+\n+", "_diff_cache": null}}
